#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""camera_calib — D435 depth accuracy check, self-calibration and settings.

The robot's lidar is the tape measure: it measures walls to about a
centimetre, so the D435 depth can be checked against it and the camera can
be calibrated without the RealSense Viewer and without a person measuring.

  check       live comparison depth - lidar on the same surfaces (~4 s,
              camera keeps running). A stereo disparity bias grows with
              z^2 (dz = z^2 * dd / (f * B)), so the result is the fit
              depth - lidar = k * z^2, shown at 1 / 2 / 3 m.
  watch       scene check for the calibration wizard (2 Hz while the UI
              asks): a flat wall in the middle of the image, 0.6-2.0 m,
              seen by the lidar, robot standing still.
  calibrate   1. scene + check before (ROS)
              2. ROS camera paused (/d435/enable false), the camera opened
                 through librealsense (pyrealsense2)
              3. backup of the calibration table from flash
              4. on-chip calibration (depth noise) and tare (absolute
                 distance; ground truth = the wall plane from the lidar,
                 or a tape measure from the UI), both in the camera's RAM
              5. ROS camera back, check after
              6. better -> written to the camera (EEPROM), else the old
                 table is put back (flash was never touched)
  restore     the backup from before the last saved calibration -> EEPROM
  factory     the camera's factory calibration -> EEPROM
  set / reset_settings
              live D435 settings (emitter, laser power, auto exposure,
              white balance) through dynamic_reconfigure, remembered in
              ~/.vitulus/camera/settings.json and applied again whenever the
              camera (re)starts

Never moves the robot. Calibration refuses while the robot moves or a mowing
program runs; the camera is paused for about a minute (no camera obstacles).

Topics (rosbridge friendly):
  ~cmd     std_msgs/String  JSON {"cmd": "check" | "watch" | "calibrate" |
                            "cancel" | "restore" | "factory" | "set" |
                            "reset_settings", ...}
  ~status  std_msgs/String  JSON, latched (see Node.status())
"""
